##
    A number too large to hold.

    This program compiles. Integer arithmetic is checked, so a result that will not fit stops
    the program rather than wrapping round to a wrong answer that looks plausible.

    20 factorial is the largest that fits in an integer. 21 factorial is not.
##

shared model Program

    function Main()
        for n = 18 to 21
            Console.WriteLine(n + "! = " + Program.Factorial(n));
        end for
    end function

    integer function Factorial(integer n)
        integer product = 1;

        for factor = 2 to n
            product = product * factor;
        end for

        yield product;
    end function

end model
